  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "End-plug electrostatic confinement at mirror ratio 10+ produces a potential barrier deep enough to confine main-cell D-T ions at Q > 5",
      "Linear ~7 MW/m center-cell scaling holds such that fusion power grows with length while end-plug input power remains roughly constant",
      "DCLC and Alfvén ion cyclotron instabilities can be actively stabilized via sloshing ions and vortex flows at commercial density and temperature",
      "HTS REBCO axisymmetric solenoids survive 14 MeV neutron flux over 30-year plant life with tractable shielding and demountable connections",
      "Venetian-blind direct energy converter electrodes survive continuous D-T exhaust bombardment and deliver ~54% conversion of the ~20% alpha-particle energy fraction",
      "A lithium-based blanket around the cylindrical center cell achieves TBR > 1 at 14 MeV neutron fluence",
      "Steady-state NBI + ECH heating sustains end-plug plasma with a recirculating power fraction low enough to keep Qe > 1"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No disruption-mitigation structure or vacuum vessel hardening — linear mirror has no plasma current and therefore no disruptions",
      "No 3D shaped saddle or yin-yang coils — axisymmetric solenoids are simpler and cheaper to wind than tokamak D-coils or stellarator coils",
      "No minimum-ignition plasma volume constraint — linear geometry claims to avoid the large-plant size floor that drives tokamak capital cost",
      "Reduced end-region port-area fraction — the 50+ meter center cell allows NBI penetrations without large fractional surface-area penalty",
      "No pulsed-magnetic-compression capacitor bank and its 10^9-shot reliability burden (as required by pulsed linear concepts like Helion)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Venetian-blind direct energy converter assembly, including magnetic field expansion hardware and periodic electrode replacement from fusion-exhaust erosion",
      "Long linear building and civil structure scaling with 50–70+ m center-cell length rather than a compact tokamak footprint",
      "Hot-cell remote-handling infrastructure along the full length of a linear machine for activated center-cell module replacement",
      "Center-cell solenoid modules with demountable connections and per-module radiation shielding distributed across tens of meters",
      "Continuous (not pulsed) high-power NBI + ECH heating plant sized for steady-state end-plug sustainment, including ~$1M/MW gyrotrons at 40–100 MW class"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "End-plug confinement at Q > 5 has never been experimentally validated; Anvil demonstrator (~2028) is the first dedicated test, and failure would roughly double required fusion and input power",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Recirculating power fraction is unpublished and the two parametric models disagree by 2.5× (40 vs 100 MW input), which directly determines whether Qe > 1 is achievable",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Per-meter cost of the center cell (magnets, building, blanket) has never been estimated, so the linear-scaling economic thesis is physically plausible but uncosted",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "DCLC and Alfvén ion cyclotron instabilities require active stabilization still being developed computationally; degraded stabilization reduces achievable Q substantially",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket architecture (FLiBe, LiPb, liquid Li, HCPB) is undisclosed, driving 36–45% thermal efficiency range, TBR uncertainty, and blanket capital cost uncertainty",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "TBR > 1 has never been validated under 14 MeV fusion-neutron flux for any blanket concept, and Li-6 enrichment is dominated by Russian/Chinese supply",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "DEC electrode survivability under continuous D-T exhaust (neutrons, energetic neutrals, alphas) is undemonstrated over commercial lifetime, and the thin uncooled electrode design is not analyzed in Realta's published materials",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape supply chain is thin (single-supplier concentration with CFS) and current $30–100/kA-m pricing must fall ~10× to reach commercial viability",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium startup inventory (~1 kg likely) must come from a global ~25–30 kg CANDU-derived supply at >$35,000/g, a fleet-level constraint",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "End divertor heat flux and handling strategy at commercial fusion power has not been analyzed in any Realta or recent mirror publication",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Hot-cell remote handling along a 50–70 m linear machine for activated center-cell module replacement is a known practical concern not addressed in Realta materials, with direct capacity-factor implications",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "DEC thermodynamic contribution in D-T is capped at ~11% of thermal output (20% alpha fraction × 54% efficiency), so the touted differentiator provides only 10–15% LCOE swing",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Commercial Hammir center-cell length is unspecified; 50 m pilot targets Q > 5 but Q >> 5 and Pe >> 50 MWe require longer unspecified configurations",
        "severity": "medium"
      }
    ]
  },
